==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|sit upon}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-sit on.ogg|a=AU}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|<,,sat>}} {{tlb|en|transitive}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|idiomatic}} To [[block]], [[suppress]], [[restrain]] (something).
#: {{ux|en|The chairman '''sat on''' the report until the end of the legislative session.}}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic|informal}} To [[restrain]] (a person).
#: {{ux|en|He started to act up, but she '''sat on''' him.}}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To take no action on (something); to hold (something) in reserve without actually using.
#: {{ux|en|I sent the boss my proposal three weeks ago and he's just been '''sitting on''' it.}}
# To be a member of (something).
#: {{ux|en|He '''sits on''' the appropriations committee.}}
# To hold an official inquiry regarding (something); to [[deliberate]] about (something).
# {{lb|en|euphemism}} To [[insert]] (something) into one's [[vagina]] or [[anus]] from below.
#: {{ux|en|Let me '''sit on''' it.}}
# {{&lit|en|sit|on}}
#: {{ux|en|The cat '''sat on''' the mat.}}

